      "writtenOn": "2023-09-29T18:17:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this will solve the issue at hand, though I\u0027m curious the design trade-off between always shaving a packet off at the end if we extend past the desired size vs. just-in-time checking the size, removing as needed, and then re-adding the packet. I _feel like_ this is what the code was going for, but that return statement kept it from continuing to write the packet to the queue (or they forgot). Heck, they even returned the wrong, larger size, which implies to me either its an honest bug, or someone sometime thought \"oh, we\u0027re removing and then writing, so its the same size.\" Again, not totally sure though 😊",
      "revId": "631ffd4f12139f5903fa28bbb8625c0ba105cb1c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "750e4013_52e234d8",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1427525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-02T15:59:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We talked offline-- I\u0027ll leave it up to you whether you want to do the \"remove the last packet if needed\" or \"always remove the last packet when we\u0027re full\" strategy. Both will work, and both address this otherwise rare issue.",
      "revId": "631ffd4f12139f5903fa28bbb8625c0ba105cb1c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aead01a2_bd191e33",
        "filename": "system/btif/src/btif_a2dp_sink.cc",
